# What the `functions/` codebase imports directly. Not read by any install: the installs use requirements.lock, the
# full resolved set with hashes, made from this file universal from Python 3.12 up (the Cloud Functions python312 image, a
# Windows PC), never from a PC's own environment (docs/backend.md → The lock file):
#   uv pip compile functions/requirements.in --universal --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes --output-file functions/requirements.lock
# A new version of pymupdf, python-bidi or Pillow changes the PDFs' bytes: it needs a new builder version (functions/builders/).
firebase-functions
firebase-admin
pymupdf
python-bidi
Pillow
huggingface_hub>=1.0  # the private training-data bucket (datastore.py), once the server has its token
numpy  # the firm stamp's cleaning (seal.py)
